<title>SINGAPORE: Marubeni to win Sri Lanka naphtha at minus $0.62.</title>
<headline>Marubeni to win Sri Lanka naphtha at minus $0.62.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's state-owned Ceylon Petroleum Corp (CPC) is to award its naphtha sell tender to Japanese trader Marubeni at 62 cents a barrel below Singapore spot quotes, free-on-board (fob) Colombo lifting November 28-29, a CPC official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The official said the tender for 125,000 barrels of light naphtha which closed 1530 hours Sri Lanka time on November 13, would be awarded by around 1830 hours November 14.</p>
<p>CPC sold its last naphtha cargo of 120,000 barrels lifting October 19-20 at $1.18 per barrel below Singapore quotes, fob.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
